WEBVTT

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:01.580
Welcome back.

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.660
Today I thought we'd do a little picture

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:05.760
that's a little different than what we've been doing.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.700
And today I want to emphasize how to do

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.580
several ranges of mountains and have some in the background

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:13.860
that are very quiet, very distant,

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:15.600
and then come forward with it,

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:17.040
and we'll see what happens here.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:18.760
I've already prepared the canvas

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.920
with a layer of magic white,

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.540
just brushed in both directions.

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:25.930
Okay, we'll start with a little bit of Prussian blue,

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:29.430
and we're really working into the bristles of the brush.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:35.680
and we'll start right at the top, working across.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:38.340
And we're picking up the magic light

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:41.920
as we go across here, automatically.

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:44.890
It makes the sky get lighter as it works downward.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:49.560
We don't want a sky that just looks like

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:50.500
you pulled the curtain down.

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:51.740
We're trying to avoid those.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:59.060
We'll hypnotize it a little bit.

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:05.900
Then while we've got some blue on the brush here,

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:10.640
we might as well go ahead and put in a little bit of water here.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:14.680
This is still the prussian blue.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:23.530
Add this a little bit, bring it all together.

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:27.690
It really doesn't matter where you get your water line here

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:29.980
because when you put all the other stuff in, you can...

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:32.470
at whatever point you want it, so don't worry about it.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:41.800
Okay, we'll wash this old brush.

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:49.290
Alrighty, let's take some blue,

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:50.920
and a little bit of brown,

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:54.920
and a little bit of white,

00:01:58.680 --> 00:01:59.980
just to make sort of a gray color.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:04.170
blue-gray here, and maybe we're gonna have this mountain

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:06.850
come way up on the canvas, what the heck.

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:10.350
And just let it roll around.

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:21.250
A little paint, and we're pushing that paint

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:24.760
right into the canvas, just really push it.

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:28.660
Put a little bump right there, another little hill.

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:38.380
I'm gonna take and pull that paint down.

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:40.660
We want it to get lighter as it goes

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:43.980
toward the horizon here, so we pull it down.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:46.560
Once again, it's mixing with the magic white

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:47.600
that's already on the canvas,

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:49.180
and automatically this occurs.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:54.080
This one down a little.

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:05.160
Now this time we want very little paint, very little paint.

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:08.460
All we want to do is give little indications back here.

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:15.060
Just a little, a few little highlights.

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:27.600
Find if you're right-handed,

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:29.970
it's normally easier to have the light.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:30.900
coming from the right.

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:34.780
If you're left-handed, it will vary from person to person.

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:38.130
So you sort of have to find what's comfortable for you.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:43.230
Maybe a little speck of light back here on that point.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.060
Maybe we'll just let these two

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:57.000
sort of work their way together here.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:04.300
Let's make an almighty ridge coming right through there.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:17.770
Now, shadow, we'll use a little blue and white,

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:19.600
a little touch of brown with it.

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:22.040
Let's put a little shadow right here.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:25.980
Don't want a great deal in the shadows this time.

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:28.220
Just, just a little bit.

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:38.550
Maybe a little touch over in here.

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:46.480
A few little things happening all along the way.

00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:03.080
A little bit too straight, so I'm gonna break that up a little

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:05.090
so it doesn't look too round.

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:07.950
I don't want it to look phony, I want it to look real.

00:05:11.980 --> 00:05:14.160
Okay, now I'm gonna really diffuse this one.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:15.720
I want it to just about disappear.

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:29.650
I'm gonna work a little bit in there, upward.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:34.920
Always follow the angles that you've built in your mountain.

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:37.340
Always work with those angles.

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:52.120
Okay, now let's build another one a little closer.

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:55.200
This time I'm gonna put a little alizarin in blue

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:58.560
to give it a little bit more of a purplish hue.

00:05:58.980 --> 00:05:59.920
A little touch of brown.

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:11.640
Let's this one and run right up through here.

00:06:13.170 --> 00:06:15.680
This being so dark should push everything back.

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:27.500
This has to be a nice slow rolling little hill.

00:06:36.140 --> 00:06:37.240
Then just get in there and do it.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:38.980
Don't worry about it.

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:39.560
Let it happen.

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:48.460
It's down a little bit.

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:58.080
One reason we do so many mountains in this series

00:06:58.080 --> 00:06:59.960
is to teach you to use the knife.

00:07:00.410 --> 00:07:03.300
You can make mountains, you've made friends with a knife.

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:05.740
Then you can do just about anything you wanna do with it.

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:14.070
Okay, maybe we'll take a little blue and white here.

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:18.880
Maybe there's a few little patches of snow laying on this.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:19.800
Just here and there.

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:24.580
Just let those work down here and there.

00:07:33.070 --> 00:07:34.870
Maybe there's a little snow laying right in here

00:07:34.870 --> 00:07:56.730
so I'm gonna sort of bring that together.

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:28.690
A little bit of the blue and brown.

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:33.170
And put some sap green with it.

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:44.570
It's very dark.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:45.550
It should look black.

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:53.160
Load the brush up.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:01.880
We'll just do some little things like this.

00:09:02.690 --> 00:09:05.140
I want some little indication of trees,

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:07.140
way back in the distance back here.

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:28.870
A few of them have just a little bit more detail,

00:09:29.030 --> 00:09:29.970
so we can just add a little.

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:30.960
a little bit here and there.

00:09:31.770 --> 00:09:34.170
We're only looking for basic shapes as far back.

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:35.910
You would not see a great deal of detail.

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:41.900
Here and there, a nice little tree

00:09:41.900 --> 00:09:43.810
that's got a little more shape.

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:02.870
A lot of paint on the brush. Very, very thick.

00:10:38.120 --> 00:10:38.860
Just like so.

00:10:41.630 --> 00:10:46.150
Now then, we can take and just scratch a few little trunks here and there.

00:10:48.320 --> 00:10:52.940
What we're doing here is using the point of the knife

00:10:52.940 --> 00:10:55.750
and cutting through the paint so the canvas shows.

00:10:56.950 --> 00:10:59.150
Gives the illusion of little trunks.

00:11:00.250 --> 00:11:09.400
And you don't have to worry about cutting through the canvas with this knife.

00:11:10.220 --> 00:11:11.440
The canvas is very, very strong.

00:11:11.740 --> 00:11:15.170
And we recommend that you use stretch canvas rather than canvas boards.

00:11:15.310 --> 00:11:18.340
The canvas boards have cardboard in the center,

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:22.500
and they have a tendency to absorb your magic white very rapidly

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:24.260
and leave you with a dry canvas.

00:11:24.460 --> 00:11:28.050
We depend on this being wet through the whole picture.

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:37.260
Now let's take a little green, a little yellow,

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:38.660
red all mixed together here,

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:42.770
and let's start putting some land coming down through here.

00:11:44.060 --> 00:11:45.380
And all we're gonna do is just push

00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:59.340
all the little grassy things happening here.

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:17.310
and maybe here and there,

00:12:17.480 --> 00:12:22.230
we can see little parts of the dirt showing through,

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:24.770
little areas where there's some ground showing.

00:12:25.770 --> 00:12:26.770
Can we just lay that in?

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:34.730
And you can just go back and sort of push it down

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:37.170
into the picture, put things that are projecting over it.

00:12:38.430 --> 00:12:40.420
A little more magic here.

00:12:40.940 --> 00:12:43.340
I have to have a thin paint to make it stick on all this.

00:12:43.460 --> 00:12:53.740
And as these come out of the shadow,

00:12:53.860 --> 00:12:54.740
let them get a little brighter.

00:12:56.490 --> 00:12:58.330
These trees would shadow all back in there,

00:12:58.370 --> 00:12:59.850
so you want this to get a little brighter.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:00.600
as it comes out.

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:08.780
Okay.

00:13:09.830 --> 00:13:12.070
Now let's take and pull just a little bit of this

00:13:12.070 --> 00:13:13.780
down into the water.

00:13:34.510 --> 00:13:38.220
And then we'll just, just hypnotize it a little bit,

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:40.340
just to sort of make it come together.

00:13:45.530 --> 00:13:47.150
Here I'm adding just a little bit of dark.

00:13:47.270 --> 00:13:48.590
We have two light areas,

00:13:48.690 --> 00:13:50.270
so we'll put a touch of dark in here,

00:13:50.670 --> 00:13:51.990
just to separate these.

00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:55.360
Very, very little paint.

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:09.550
Let's take a little Van Dyke Brown,

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:16.580
and just go right along here and build us a little shore.

00:14:17.800 --> 00:14:19.900
Here, all we're doing is touching the canvas.

00:14:34.730 --> 00:14:35.710
There's a few little sticks in here

00:14:35.710 --> 00:14:37.130
where we have some color on the knife.

00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:48.070
You know, when people see all these little sticks and stuff,

00:14:48.110 --> 00:14:50.830
they think you spent days and days with your one-haired brush

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:53.070
sitting here doing all these little rascals.

00:14:53.290 --> 00:14:54.750
And when you get them believing that,

00:14:54.950 --> 00:14:56.620
then you up the price of it.

00:15:02.910 --> 00:15:04.990
For a long time, I painted this way in the secrecy

00:15:04.990 --> 00:15:07.450
of my home and charged unbelievable prices,

00:15:08.130 --> 00:15:09.550
which a lot of painters are doing now.

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:16.990
But if people see it takes you 30 minutes,

00:15:17.030 --> 00:15:19.770
then they don't want to pay you an unbelievable price for it.

00:15:19.790 --> 00:15:21.190
They want to pay you 30 minutes of labor.

00:15:21.470 --> 00:15:23.580
So, you have to make a decision

00:15:23.580 --> 00:15:25.900
whether you want to be a traditional artist

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:27.700
or an artist that eats regular.

00:15:36.460 --> 00:15:38.700
Maybe we'll lay some little ripples along the water here.

00:15:57.780 --> 00:15:59.740
Maybe we'll take some of this dark color.

00:16:02.430 --> 00:16:05.560
And let's put a little tree right here.

00:16:05.700 --> 00:16:06.240
What the heck?

00:16:19.890 --> 00:16:21.470
Take and pull some of that paint down,

00:16:21.630 --> 00:16:22.670
make this a little reflection.

00:16:30.410 --> 00:16:31.650
Put a little tree trunk in,

00:16:37.670 --> 00:16:42.330
highlight right along here, just so he stands out.

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:49.450
Then he needs some leaves on him,

00:16:49.510 --> 00:16:51.450
so I'm gonna drop a few little leaves here and there.

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:40.360
I'm going to destroy just a little bit of the dandyke here.

00:18:00.920 --> 00:18:02.280
Let's put something in the foreground.

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:05.900
We'll have all kind of nice little bushes and stuff

00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:07.520
just growing around here.

00:18:08.530 --> 00:18:14.760
Put something right here.

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:39.480
And we'll highlight these real quick.

00:19:02.560 --> 00:19:04.850
Look at that, all those little leaves and bushes.

00:19:06.350 --> 00:19:09.050
You can do it, you can do it.

00:19:09.170 --> 00:19:13.300
Just practice a little, load a lot of paint into the brush.

00:19:14.230 --> 00:19:16.210
Remember, thin paint will stick to a thick paint.

00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:48.420
Maybe just less little sticks.

00:20:26.560 --> 00:20:29.970
Let's have a huge limb coming out here, like there's a tree over here.

00:20:30.030 --> 00:20:31.650
here somewhere and all you can see

00:20:31.650 --> 00:20:33.610
is the big limb coming out.

00:20:34.760 --> 00:20:39.030
I know this is scary to take and put something like this

00:20:39.030 --> 00:20:40.890
right out through all the work you went through,

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:43.120
but give it a try one time.

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:49.330
Maybe we have one coming down through here.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:02.310
I have some little limbs coming off these.

00:21:16.390 --> 00:21:18.190
Wherever you want them, just drop them in.

00:21:24.950 --> 00:21:27.090
There's a little something just protruding right up here.

00:21:31.440 --> 00:21:40.390
Just a little bit of highlight on here just to break it up

00:21:40.390 --> 00:21:43.380
until a little sunlight's hitting.

00:21:59.310 --> 00:21:59.790
Let's lace.

00:22:00.380 --> 00:22:01.160
leaves on top of that.

00:22:04.260 --> 00:22:06.900
First need some dark, get some dark color here.

00:22:08.270 --> 00:22:10.650
A little bit of sap, a little bit of blue and brown.

00:22:10.970 --> 00:22:18.940
You can lay a little color on the brush here.

00:22:20.140 --> 00:22:23.140
Now we're just gonna start tapping

00:22:23.140 --> 00:22:25.460
where we want some nice little leaves to be.

00:22:31.560 --> 00:22:32.900
Just let them fall in there.

00:22:43.830 --> 00:22:46.290
This sort of helps make a nice composition of your picture

00:22:46.290 --> 00:22:47.510
and push everything back.

00:22:51.810 --> 00:22:53.390
Think you'll like this once you try it.

00:23:01.340 --> 00:23:05.920
I mean, as I say, first time it's sort of a son of a gun just to throw all this right out the middle of your picture.

00:23:06.100 --> 00:23:07.340
It's going to scare you a little bit.

00:23:07.760 --> 00:23:09.070
But jump in there and do it.

00:23:10.580 --> 00:23:11.620
Remember, you're the master.

00:23:12.760 --> 00:23:14.240
This canvas is afraid of you.

00:23:14.400 --> 00:23:15.280
You're the master.

00:23:15.800 --> 00:23:29.980
You can take lighter color green, a little more...

00:23:30.190 --> 00:23:36.540
Magic in it, and load this brush well.

00:23:37.200 --> 00:23:38.540
And think where your light's coming from.

00:23:38.620 --> 00:23:40.680
The top of these are gonna be a little brighter

00:23:40.680 --> 00:23:42.880
than the bottom, so we'll just lay a little bit

00:23:42.880 --> 00:23:44.360
of color right along the top here.

00:23:48.790 --> 00:23:50.370
This is where you need a good brush, though.

00:23:53.150 --> 00:23:55.150
Very careful about the brush you use.

00:23:55.590 --> 00:23:57.870
Avoid nylon brushes, they cut paint.

00:23:58.990 --> 00:23:59.970
These are natural bristles.

00:24:00.060 --> 00:24:26.690
brushes please remember back when i was a traditional painter along i would agonize

00:24:26.690 --> 00:24:29.720
trying to do something like this with a little one-haired brush

00:24:31.020 --> 00:24:33.180
working for days and days and days to get an effect

00:24:33.180 --> 00:24:34.740
that you can now get in minutes.

00:25:00.320 --> 00:25:02.800
Almighty limbs projecting right out in our picture.

00:25:03.240 --> 00:25:05.020
And it makes it look like there's a tree over here.

00:25:06.330 --> 00:25:11.000
Okay, maybe, maybe right in here.

00:25:11.100 --> 00:25:11.920
Let's do this.

00:25:12.640 --> 00:25:14.500
Let's have an old tree that's falling over,

00:25:15.810 --> 00:25:16.910
coming right up through here.

00:25:17.960 --> 00:25:20.420
If you got all your nerve up and done this one,

00:25:21.600 --> 00:25:23.440
shoot, we might as well just keep going with it.

00:25:25.310 --> 00:25:26.610
No use letting you stop now.

00:25:34.440 --> 00:25:36.800
and maybe he had a little friend that fell over with him.

00:25:36.980 --> 00:25:46.240
But don't laugh, trees need friends too,

00:25:46.340 --> 00:25:47.400
everybody needs friends.

00:25:52.350 --> 00:25:57.780
A little white and a little brown here.

00:26:01.150 --> 00:26:02.650
Maybe we'll put just at least a little touch

00:26:02.650 --> 00:26:06.000
of sort of an orangey color in it.

00:26:08.740 --> 00:26:10.640
Just work that right down here

00:26:10.640 --> 00:26:15.440
and make him look old and tired, just barely touching.

00:26:20.120 --> 00:26:24.780
Just pull that right along, like so, yeah.

00:26:28.100 --> 00:26:29.260
Okay, now we'll take...

00:26:31.280 --> 00:26:33.020
And put a few little bushes in front

00:26:33.020 --> 00:26:36.180
so he has a place for his foots to set.

00:26:38.190 --> 00:26:39.550
And we'll take the liner brush,

00:26:40.000 --> 00:26:44.510
a little bit of thin oil, like so, there we go.

00:26:47.080 --> 00:26:49.440
And we'll put a few little limbs hanging on here

00:26:49.440 --> 00:26:53.160
that are just about going, just here and there.

00:26:55.250 --> 00:26:57.350
Let them go every which way, whatever makes them happy.

00:27:04.090 --> 00:27:05.890
And maybe this one's just hanging down.

00:27:06.030 --> 00:27:08.680
Ooh, he's tired. Poor old thing.

00:27:16.220 --> 00:27:18.120
Tree's just about going.

00:27:18.260 --> 00:27:20.400
It's going to fall over here in the pond.

00:27:24.740 --> 00:27:26.460
Maybe a little limb or two left up here.

00:27:31.850 --> 00:27:32.710
Something like so.

00:27:39.860 --> 00:27:43.460
Okay, I think we'll sign that one and call it finished.

00:27:44.930 --> 00:27:46.520
And there we go.

00:27:47.620 --> 00:27:49.300
And I'd like to thank you very, very much

00:27:49.300 --> 00:27:50.360
for watching us today.

00:27:50.920 --> 00:27:52.460
I hope you've enjoyed this painting

00:27:52.460 --> 00:27:54.520
and that you've painted along with us.

00:27:54.700 --> 00:27:56.640
And until next time, happy painting.

00:27:56.800 --> 00:27:57.740
Thank you very, very much.
